    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n### 1: Fetch & Parse New Blog Post Data\n- **Generate & Fetch Pages:**  \n  Iterates through blog page numbers, fetching each page’s content for processing.\n- **Extract and Aggregate Content:**  \n  Parses blog posts from the raw HTML response and aggregates the data into a unified JSON format.\n- **Parse Blog Details:**  \n  Breaks down each blog entry into structured components suitable for storage.\n\n### 2: Retrieve Existing Data \n  Retrieves current table values to check for already stored blog posts, ensuring that the workflow processes only new or updated entries.\n\n### Compare & Merge Data from 1 & 2\n- **Append Unique Blog Posts:**  \n  Compares new entries (from 1) with existing records (from 2) to avoid duplicates, then appends only fresh blog post content to the PostgresSQL table or Qdrant Vector Store collection.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 680,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        560,
        540
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "430d22aa-5f31-407d-a864-a9b7a1111b96",
      "name": "Sticky Note3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Storage Methods\n- **Store Data in PostgreSQL:**  \n  Persists validated blog posts in a PostgreSQL database for reliable, structured, and transactional storage.\n- **Generate and Store Embeddings:**  \n  Converts blog text into vector embeddings and saves them in a Qdrant Vector Store, enabling efficient semantic searching.\n",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1900,
        260
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "3f66d893-0925-4989-b633-e1b92cac61b7",
      "name": "Sticky Note4"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "This AI agent answers queries about Bitovi's blog articles using a **dual-retrieval strategy**.\n\n### Retrieval Methods\n- **PostgreSQL Retriever:**  \n  Activated when queries include metadata hints (e.g., \"latest,\" \"by category,\" \"by author,\" or specific dates). It performs structured queries on the `blog_posts` database to fetch precise data.\n- **Vector Store Embeddings Retriever:**  \n  Used for open-ended queries. It leverages semantic similarity via vector embeddings to retrieve contextually relevant blog excerpts from `bitovi_blog` collection.\n\n### Workflow Overview\n1. **Intent Analysis:**  \n   The agent inspects the user's query for metadata indicators.\n2. **Retriever Selection:**  \n   - **Metadata-related queries:** Uses the PostgreSQL retriever.\n   - **General or open-ended queries:** Uses the Vector Store Embeddings retriever.\n3. **Response Generation:**  \n   The answer is constructed solely from the fetched blog content and enriched with relevant metadata (date, category, author, title). If no context is found, the agent replies with:\n   > \"I couldn’t find relevant information in the blog articles.\"\n\nThis dual approach ensures precise filtering and comprehensive semantic matching for accurate, context-aware responses.\n",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
